<center><h2>The Art of Tempering Spices (Tadka)</h2></center>

<h3>Ingredients</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>1.5 tbsp ghee or cooking oil</li>
    <li>1 tsp cumin seeds (jeera)</li>
    <li>1 tsp mustard seeds (rai)</li>
    <li>1/4 tsp asafoetida (hing)</li>
    <li>8 to 10 fresh curry leaves</li>
    <li>1 to 2 dried whole red chilies</li>
    <li>3 to 4 cloves garlic, thinly sliced</li>
    <li>1/2 tsp Kashmiri red chili powder (optional)</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Instructions</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Warm the ghee or oil in a small pan over medium heat until shimmering.</li>
    <li>Add mustard seeds and cumin seeds, cooking for 15 to 20 seconds until they pop and turn fragrant.</li>
    <li>Reduce heat slightly and sauté sliced garlic and whole red chilies for 20 to 30 seconds until lightly golden.</li>
    <li>Add curry leaves and asafoetida carefully as they sizzle.</li>
    <li>Take the pan off the heat, stir in Kashmiri red chili powder if using, and pour the hot tempering immediately over your dish.</li>
  </ol>
  
  

